  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with the front matter that the `skills` site query recognizes, so `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow` applies.\n\nThe requirement says each skill must open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. The file has one H1, `# Habeas`. A short orientation passage comes first, and it has no heading of its own. It is part of the title block, not a separate section. The first `##` section is `## Workflow`, which is `section[Habeas]/section[Workflow]`. Every other section follows it: Testing and coverage artifacts, Inspecting, Requirements/examples/definitions, References and Gotchas. So no other section precedes the workflow.\n\nThe workflow is an ordered checklist, `- [ ] 1.` (pick the skill from the table) and `- [ ] 2.` (follow that skill, with the move-then-edit rule). The steps are numbered consecutively.\n\nThe requirement's test, `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_open_with_their_workflow_as_ordered_steps]`, uses the same reading. It requires the first `## ` heading to be `## Workflow` and the step numbers to run 1..n with at least two steps. This file meets that.\n\nThere is no violation query in the requirement, so there are no violation matches to judge. I found no gap.",
